youtube-tba-upload

This project is derived from TBA-uploader by lethosor
(https://github.com/lethosor/TBA-uploader), by way of Filip-Kin/TBA-uploader.

The following originate upstream and remain under the upstream license (see the
LICENSE file, which is carried unchanged):
  - the autoav-helper YouTube uploader (now this module's main package),
  - internal/ytstudio (the chromedp YouTube Studio automation), and
  - the tba package (trusted-API request signing).

Changes made here:
  - extracted the uploader into a standalone Go module,
  - replaced the JSON state file with a shared SQLite database (WAL) that FIM-AV
    Assistant and this sidecar both use,
  - added TBA match_videos/add submission after upload, plus /api/health and
    /api/shutdown for running as a managed sidecar.
